<title>FRANCE: London tops key EU airport cargo growth in.</title>
<headline>London tops key EU airport cargo growth in.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London airports had the highest cargo traffic growth amongst the EU's top cargo airports in March and for January-March 1997 compared to the same 1996 period, figures issued by the Paris airports authority (ADP) show.</p>
<p>			     Mar 1997		Pct change</p>
<p>			    (in tonnes)	    on March 96</p>
<p>     London*	     138,900		 up  8.5</p>
<p>     Frankfurt	   127,400		 up  7.8</p>
<p>     Amsterdam	   107,100		 up  6.4</p>
<p>     Paris**	     103,114		 up  2.8</p>
<p>			     Jan-Mar 1997	   Pct change</p>
<p>			     (in tonnes)	    on Jan-Mar 96</p>
<p>     London*	     367,103		  up  8.1</p>
<p>     Frankfurt	   329,448		  up  4.7</p>
<p>     Amsterdam	   280,457		  up  3.9</p>
<p>     Paris**	     273,110		  up  2.6</p>
<p>*  includes Heathrow, Gatwick, Stansted and all are part of the BAA Plc</p>
<p>	 group.</p>
<p>** includes Charles de Gaulle and Orly -Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542-7706 Fax+-5017</p>
